module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.instrument_refusal_before_subject_reads_as_a_subject_verdict

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data instrument_refusal_before_subject_reads_as_a_subject_verdict: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "instrument_refusal_before_subject_reads_as_a_subject_verdict" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an instrument's report is consumed as a verdict about its subject while the run refused before ever reaching that subject** (INVALID STATE: an instrument report whose citing consumers cannot distinguish REFUSED BEFORE REACHING THE SUBJECT from SUBJECT VERDICT. The report is a Bool, or a success/exit pair, and the refusal of an admission the instrument had to pass on the way in -- here the compiler's workspace-root admission of the staged tree -- collapses into the same false, or the same pass on an expect-failure arm, that a real finding about the subject would produce. HARM: the instrument is cited as coverage of its subject for as long as it stays enrolled, and it measures nothing. A green reads as the subject holding; a red reads as the subject broken, and is then 'known red' and stops being looked at, while the actual cause is an admission the subject never reached.)",

    "THE DISTINGUISHING FACT: the refusal cause is the workspace-root admission of a /tmp stage, never the subject. Four instruments stage their subject with a bare shell.Mktemp.Dir, which lands outside the checkout, and the compiler refuses such a stage before resolving anything -- 'primary source root is outside the workspace root' on a whole-root argv, 'entry file is outside the workspace root' on an --entry argv. Staged under the workspace, the same compiles run to their subject: the staged std.logic compile exits 0 with one file emitted, and the cross-tree import green exits 0 with zero blocking errors. The subject was never the cause.",

    "THE RECEIPTS, by instrument name, from the per-instrument table on gunbc#11265 (session nimble-badger-98, 2026-09-13, session container, v1 binary built from that PR's tree, head 45f91bd9c94): test.claim.dag_compile_clean_seam_witness cross_shard_seam_preservation_holds_on_live_tree returns false; test.claim.dag_compile_clean_shard_a_witness compile_clean_shard_a_exemplar_compile_green returns false; test.claim.long.dag_compile_clean_perturb_corpus perturb_cross_tree_import_corpus_green_holds and perturb_dag_shell_primary_corpus_green_holds each return false. THE PRE-EXISTING CONTROL: on the pre-change binary (built from gunbc#11227's tree, where whole-root admission was still a population-blind constant and no instrument argv had changed), the shard exemplar's own argv over a /tmp stage refuses at root-admission as outside the workspace root, so these four were refusing before that PR and the PR neither caused nor repaired them. THE DISCRIMINATING CONTROL BESIDE THEM: test.claim.dag_compile_clean_perturb_receipts perturb_fixture_green_holds returns true, and so do its two reds, because tools.dag_compile_clean_transport dcc_fixture_perturb_compile_expecting stages under target/ inside the workspace. Same transport, same compile shape, one variable -- where the stage lives -- and opposite outcomes.",

    "WHY THE REDS ARE THE DANGEROUS HALF, AND NOT THE GREENS. An expect-failure arm over a stage the compiler refuses PASSES whatever the subject is: the refusal satisfies 'the compile must fail'. The perturb reds in this population happen to stage inside the workspace and so do reach their subject; any red that staged in /tmp would read as a held wall while testing nothing. The same collapse makes a green unreachable and a red vacuous, so neither direction of the report can be trusted without knowing which admission refused.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[an_unreached_measurement_renders_as_a_failed_one]], THE NEAREST ROW, which shares the shape 'never reached its subject, reported like a verdict' and differs in carrier, rung and direction. That row's carrier is a REQUIRED LANE'S RED at the merge surface, and the distinction already exists in a typed field: the adjudication standing is present in the log, so the class sits at rung 1 and its repair is to lift the standing onto the deciding surface. It fails toward WASTE -- nothing is admitted, a red is misattributed. This row's carrier is an INSTRUMENT'S OWN REPORT, a Bool or an exit status returned to a witness, and there is no standing field anywhere to lift: the refusal and the subject verdict are the same value at birth, which is why it is found below the ladder. And it fails OPEN as well as toward waste, because an expect-failure arm turns the pre-subject refusal into a PASS. Repairing that row -- deriving the lane conclusion from its standing -- changes nothing here, since these instruments never produce a standing to derive from.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red]]: there the WITNESS FILE does not compile, so none of its assertions execute and the claim is absent. Here every witness named compiles and executes; its assertion runs and returns a value. What refuses is the compile the INSTRUMENT drives inside the run, at an admission its subject never reaches, so the witness is present, executing, and wrong about what it measured. Compiling every claim file, that row's trigger, catches none of these four.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: BELOW THE LADDER -- silent wrongness, not mitigation: a green cited as coverage for an instrument that never reached its subject is a fabricated plausible output about the compiler, and nothing typed, located or counted distinguished it. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. REASON: a report coproduct carrying the refusal as its own arm -- RefusedBeforeSubject { admission, cause } beside SubjectVerdict { ... } -- has no green constructor for a run that never reached its subject, so a consumer that matches on the report cannot mint coverage from a refusal, and the case is decidable from the executing run itself. It is not 4 because the instrument remains free to construct a SubjectVerdict wrongly; what the coproduct removes is the collapse, not every lie.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, STATED AS THE CAPABILITY AND NOT AS THE FOUR STAGES MOVING: every instrument report carries refusal-before-subject as its own typed arm, and every consumer that cites an instrument matches on that arm rather than on a Bool or an exit status. SUFFICIENT FOR: every instrument whose run passes an admission before its subject -- workspace-root admission, whole-root compile admission, budget and readiness arms -- not only these four. Moving these four stages inside the workspace root repairs the instances and fires nothing: the next instrument that stages outside, or that trips any other pre-subject refusal, is exactly as silent. That repair is owned by the v1 seed maintenance lane and is not this row's trigger.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
